00:09:29.101 --> 00:09:31.470 align:start size:97% position:3%
And now, everyone has
followed, and that's great.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.239
We're very happy about that.

00:09:33.239 --> 00:09:35.274
But like, somebody had to
stand up and take the heat.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:38.110
And at that time, there were
polls coming out last summer

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:40.479 align:start size:88% position:13%
saying that most parents
wanted mask mandates.

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:43.115 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he said, okay, that's
because they they're afraid.

00:09:43.115 --> 00:09:44.951
They're being sold
lies by the media.

00:09:44.951 --> 00:09:49.422 align:start position:0%
And they're being basically
manipulated into thinking this.

00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:52.592
And lo and behold, he was right.

00:09:52.592 --> 00:09:54.160
He had to just make a decision

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.395
that was unpopular at the time.

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:58.598 align:start size:97% position:3%
And now, everyone realizes,
like, he was right.

00:09:58.598 --> 00:10:01.133 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's what leadership
is, I think.

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:03.736
(crowd cheers)

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.241 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Don't you guys sort
of feel like he actually

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:12.411
is the president
in a way, right?

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:15.648
Like, in a way, if America's
gonna continue, he sort of,

00:10:15.648 --> 00:10:17.416
he's make, exactly.

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:20.252
Make America Florida,
I think you mean, yeah.

00:10:20.252 --> 00:10:23.522
Make America Florida, exactly.

00:10:23.522 --> 00:10:26.525
Were there ever any moments
in the heat of all of it

00:10:26.525 --> 00:10:28.628 align:start size:84% position:16%
that he almost
cracked and gave in?

00:10:28.628 --> 00:10:31.631 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because everybody was coming
after him all the time.

00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:32.832
- [Christina] No.

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:34.033 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I mean, even now,
still they're trying it.

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:35.501 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I think when people
come after him,

00:10:35.501 --> 00:10:38.504 align:start size:97% position:3%
it makes him even more
resolute in what he's doing.

00:10:38.504 --> 00:10:40.039
The more that the media attacks,

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:42.375
you saw the clip that you
ran right before, like,

00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:44.910
we started talking,
the clip about me.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:48.080 align:start size:97% position:3%
When I got attacked, he
said, you know, that's great.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.616
When Dr. Ladapo, you know,
our great surgeon general,

00:10:50.616 --> 00:10:51.550
he gets attacked.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:52.885 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Yeah.
(crowd cheers)

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:54.120
- Thank you. He's awesome.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:55.788 align:start size:88% position:13%
He gets attacked by
the media all the time.

00:10:55.788 --> 00:10:57.990 align:start size:84% position:16%
I remember, I was with
the surgeon general
and the governor,

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:00.426 align:start position:0%
and we were at a Wawa somewhere
in the middle of Florida,

00:11:00.426 --> 00:11:01.927
in Tampa Bay.

00:11:01.927 --> 00:11:03.429
And I remember in the Tampa
Bay Times, the front page

00:11:03.429 --> 00:11:05.097
was a story about Dr. Ladapo

00:11:05.097 --> 00:11:07.833 align:start position:0%
and how he's an anti-vaxxer
quack and all of this nonsense.

00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:10.169
And so, it was when he was new.

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:12.438
He wasn't confirmed yet
as a surgeon general.

00:11:12.438 --> 00:11:14.473
Like, Senate still had
to do the confirmation.

00:11:14.473 --> 00:11:16.075 align:start size:81% position:19%
So, I was a little
bit concerned.

00:11:16.075 --> 00:11:18.044
I look at the paper,
I'm like Dr. Ladapo,

00:11:18.044 --> 00:11:19.512
like, are you feeling okay?

00:11:19.512 --> 00:11:21.147 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, he just
came from California.

00:11:21.147 --> 00:11:23.082
He's not a politician.

00:11:23.082 --> 00:11:24.750
Being in the public eye
is kind of new to him.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.519
So I was like, are
you feeling okay?

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:28.187 align:start size:97% position:3%
And he's like, yeah, as
long as the governor's okay.

00:11:28.187 --> 00:11:30.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the governor said,
look, the more that people

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:33.225
are attacking Joe, that's
what he calls Dr. Ladapo,

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:35.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
the more people are
attacking Joe, the better,

00:11:35.494 --> 00:11:37.763
because that means he's
doing something right.

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:38.798
- [Dave] There you go.

00:11:38.798 --> 00:11:40.032
- And I think that's true.

00:11:42.668 --> 00:11:44.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So, speaking of
doing something right,

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.371
I think most of us can agree,

00:11:45.371 --> 00:11:47.406
we're kind of doing it
right here in Florida,

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:50.609 align:start size:88% position:13%
and people are living
free and all that stuff.

00:11:50.609 --> 00:11:52.478
Is there anything that
in Florida right now

00:11:52.478 --> 00:11:55.147
we're not doing right, or
places that the governor

00:11:55.147 --> 00:11:56.515 align:start size:84% position:16%
or the administration
is going, oh,

00:11:56.515 --> 00:11:58.050
we have to fix this or that?

00:11:59.185 --> 00:12:00.553 align:start size:84% position:16%
- [Audience Member]
School choice.

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:03.355
(audience members shout)

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:05.157
- That's a great question.

00:12:06.192 --> 00:12:07.426
Honestly -

00:12:07.426 --> 00:12:08.227
- You didn't think I
was gonna make it easy

00:12:08.227 --> 00:12:09.662
for you up here, did ya?

00:12:09.662 --> 00:12:11.297
- We can always be doing better.

00:12:11.297 --> 00:12:14.500 align:start position:0%
I think, I mean, I'm really
proud of what Florida has done,

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.802 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the example that
we are to the country.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.939
We are a leader
in school choice,

00:12:19.939 --> 00:12:21.574
could always do more on that,

00:12:21.574 --> 00:12:24.577
and I believe that'll happen.

00:12:24.577 --> 00:12:28.781
You know, there's a
lot of conservatives
come to me and say,

00:12:28.781 --> 00:12:32.418
like, constitutional carry
is a big priority for them.

00:12:32.418 --> 00:12:34.487
And that's something
the governor has said

00:12:34.487 --> 00:12:38.424 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he is committed to doing
before he leaves office.

00:12:38.424 --> 00:12:39.658
So, I believe that.

00:12:39.658 --> 00:12:41.193
I've never heard
him say something

00:12:41.193 --> 00:12:43.362 align:start size:84% position:16%
that he doesn't
follow through on, so,

00:12:43.362 --> 00:12:45.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, there are always
ways we could improve.

00:12:45.798 --> 00:12:49.135
And we're always trying
to listen to people,

00:12:49.135 --> 00:12:50.669
listen to Floridians,

00:12:50.669 --> 00:12:52.972 align:start size:88% position:13%
and look at what's going
on in other states,

00:12:52.972 --> 00:12:54.974
other countries that
we might be able to use

00:12:54.974 --> 00:12:56.642
and we might be able
to replicate here.

00:12:56.642 --> 00:12:58.577 line:0%
But I do think Florida
has been a good example

00:12:58.577 --> 00:12:59.512 line:0%
for the country.

00:12:59.512 --> 00:13:00.479 line:0%
- So what else?

00:13:00.479 --> 00:13:01.714 line:0%
Yeah, you can applaud that.

00:13:01.714 --> 00:13:03.783 line:0%
Florida has been a
pretty good example.

00:13:03.783 --> 00:13:06.619
(audience applauds)

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:09.155
What else do you think
that these folks can do

00:13:09.155 --> 00:13:12.825
to help Governor DeSantis fight
this thing, to get involved?

00:13:12.825 --> 00:13:14.860 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like, how can people,
you know, beyond voting.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.328
We get it.

00:13:16.328 --> 00:13:17.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're all gonna get
out in November and vote,

00:13:17.763 --> 00:13:19.999 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he's gonna win something
like 90% of the vote.

00:13:19.999 --> 00:13:24.003
There, you heard it
first, but, yeah.

00:13:24.003 --> 00:13:25.704 align:start size:84% position:16%
What else can people
do, do you think?

00:13:25.704 --> 00:13:28.507
- You know, but that, what
you said is really important,

00:13:28.507 --> 00:13:32.244
'cause, like, I go to a
lot of places in Florida

00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:33.479
with the governor.

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:35.214
I think he's been to all
67 counties this year.

00:13:35.214 --> 00:13:36.715
And I go to a lot
of those places,

00:13:36.715 --> 00:13:38.918
and people will come up and
say, like, how great he is

00:13:38.918 --> 00:13:41.253
and how, like, they're gonna
vote for him for president.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:43.823 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now I always say,
wait, wait, back up.

00:13:43.823 --> 00:13:44.824
He's not running for president.

00:13:44.824 --> 00:13:46.058
He's running for reelection

00:13:46.058 --> 00:13:48.027
as the governor of the
great state of Florida.

00:13:48.027 --> 00:13:50.362 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, you need to vote in
November, like, of this year.

00:13:50.362 --> 00:13:52.731
So, that's what I'm always
trying to remind people.

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:55.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
- She almost broke some
serious news here tonight.

00:13:55.301 --> 00:13:56.769
That was, we almost.

00:13:58.237 --> 00:13:59.438
- Like, we don't wanna take
anything for granted, 'cause,

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:00.739
like you said, 90% of the vote.

00:14:00.739 --> 00:14:03.209
I mean, that'd be great.
I think he deserves it.

00:14:03.209 --> 00:14:05.945
He deserves a hundred
percent, but Florida,

00:14:05.945 --> 00:14:07.746
it's always been a swing state.

00:14:07.746 --> 00:14:09.682
I believe it's becoming
more of a red state,

00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:11.750
thanks to Governor
DeSantis' leadership,

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:15.621 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we never take
anything for granted.

00:14:15.621 --> 00:14:17.122
You know, you have to always run

00:14:17.122 --> 00:14:19.625
like you're 10 points behind,
and that's what he's doing.

00:14:19.625 --> 00:14:21.093
He's working hard.

00:14:21.093 --> 00:14:24.897 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I, that's why I'm, vote
is my number one thing.

00:14:24.897 --> 00:14:27.066 align:start size:84% position:16%
Talk to your friends,
family about it.

00:14:27.066 --> 00:14:29.635
You know, don't take it for
granted that he's gonna win

00:14:29.635 --> 00:14:32.738
just because his opponents
are very weak, which is true.

00:14:32.738 --> 00:14:35.207 align:start position:0%
But like, you can't take
anything for granted, you know.

00:14:35.207 --> 00:14:36.642 align:start size:84% position:16%
You never know
what's gonna happen.

00:14:36.642 --> 00:14:39.778 align:start size:88% position:13%
So, I think that's
probably the main thing,

00:14:39.778 --> 00:14:41.547 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then, get involved
at the local level.

00:14:41.547 --> 00:14:45.017
Like, there are,
these days, I think

00:14:45.017 --> 00:14:48.454
conservatives are realizing how
important school boards are.

00:14:48.454 --> 00:14:49.822
It was never that big of a thing

00:14:49.822 --> 00:14:51.624
until the last couple of years.

00:14:51.624 --> 00:14:52.858
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:54.126 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I think parents
have realized, like,

00:14:54.126 --> 00:14:56.362
how much power they have
over your family's life,

00:14:56.362 --> 00:14:57.897
over your kids' lives,

00:14:57.897 --> 00:15:00.299
and how much they've abused
their power in some places,

00:15:00.299 --> 00:15:02.434
including here in Florida.

00:15:02.434 --> 00:15:06.338
Yeah, unfortunately,
that was one that did.

00:15:06.338 --> 00:15:07.339
- [Dave] Yep.

00:15:07.339 --> 00:15:08.741
- And there were
others, as well.

00:15:08.741 --> 00:15:13.012 align:start position:0%
And so, I think that's something
that we can learn from,

00:15:13.012 --> 00:15:14.580
and that, I know a lot
of great conservatives

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.782 align:start size:97% position:3%
are running for school
board, including in Broward

00:15:16.782 --> 00:15:19.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everywhere in Florida,
actually, this fall.

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:21.420
So, we need to replace the ones

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:23.923 align:start size:84% position:16%
that acted like petty
dictators, right?

00:15:23.923 --> 00:15:26.592 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so, getting involved
locally is important.

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:28.894
(audience applauds)

00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:30.663
- Well, I'm gonna bring
out our other two guests

00:15:30.663 --> 00:15:32.731
in a moment, who are
also great Floridians,

00:15:32.731 --> 00:15:33.999
but I just wanna say,

00:15:33.999 --> 00:15:35.234
since we got a room
full of people here,

00:15:35.234 --> 00:15:37.303
that you guys are just
doing an incredible job,

00:15:37.303 --> 00:15:40.739
and you helped me
make the move here

00:15:40.739 --> 00:15:43.409
